ormal high for the date is 45\u00b0F, and the record is 70\u00b0F (2025). The low of <strong>42\u00b0F</strong> was the 9th warmest November 13 low (tied) of 135 since 1892.","t_rec":"Record highs and lows, by the decade that set them","p_rec":"If Great Falls' climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Great Falls has set <strong>88 standing record lows</strong>, close to the 73 that chance alone would give, and <strong>99 record highs</strong>, more than the 74 that chance alone would give. The 1930s hold the most record highs of any decade (62). Great Falls' all-time high is 107\u00b0F, on July 25, 1933.","t_chg":"Great Falls' nights cooled over the long run. Its days show no clear change.","p_chg":"Across 129 complete years: Great Falls' average low has fallen <strong class='sig'>\u22120.12\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range \u22120.20 to \u22120.04), about \u22121.6\u00b0F since 1894. Great Falls' average high shows no clear change: \u22120.01\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.11 to +0.10) that includes zero.","t_mon":"Lows rose in none; 5 months fell. Highs rose in none; April fell.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Great Falls' yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (\u22120.01 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 14.7 inches a year. The wettest year was 1975 (25.24 in); the driest, 1904 (6.68 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 12 daily record highs, 4 daily record lows"}}